WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.400
Detection engineering is the discipline of creating and maintaining visibility into

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.075
suspicious,

00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:07.240
risky, or policy-relevant activity.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.000
Detection engineers design capabilities that help organizations identify threats,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.050
investigate alerts,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:16.220
and improve defensive awareness before small signals become larger problems.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.000
Although people often associate detection engineering with writing SIEM queries,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.995
the discipline is much broader.

00:00:20.995 --> 00:00:26.005
It includes telemetry planning, threat-informed design, testing, documentation, tuning,

00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:27.977
lifecycle management, measurement, and continuous improvement.

00:00:27.977 --> 00:00:29.975
A detection is not just a line of logic.

00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:33.840
It is a maintained defensive asset that depends on data quality, context,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.000
alert presentation, investigation guidance, ownership, and a plan for review.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.250
If any of those pieces are missing, analysts may receive noise instead of useful signal.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.230
Detection engineering gives security teams a repeatable way to ask important defensive

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:46.965
questions.

00:00:46.965 --> 00:00:48.000
What activity matters?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.000
What data can show it?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.000
How will the alert be tested?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.975
What should analysts do when it fires?

00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:53.965
How will the team know whether the detection is still useful?

00:00:53.965 --> 00:00:56.190
The purpose is practical.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.450
Detection engineering helps defenders turn messy operational data into meaningful

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.000
visibility,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
so teams can investigate faster, prioritize better,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.000
and learn from what they observe in their environment.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.000
A mature detection engineering program also creates shared language.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.645
Instead of debating alerts one at a time, teams can discuss coverage, fidelity, ownership,

00:01:12.645 --> 00:01:16.000
dependencies, review dates, response guidance, and measurable outcomes.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.245
That shift matters because security operations is under constant pressure.

00:01:20.245 --> 00:01:24.280
Detection engineering gives teams a structured way to improve visibility while respecting

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.570
the limits of analyst time,

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.920
platform performance, and business context.
